# Commercial S3.1 recovery compare-root abort

Date: 2026-08-29

The first S3.1 recovery-delta attempt stopped before repository synchronization,
unit installation, state repair or database bootstrap. Archive creation strips
the leading slash from absolute member names, while the following GNU tar
comparison ran from the shell working directory. The comparison therefore
looked for `etc/...` and `var/...` below the wrong directory and failed closed.

Observed partial recovery directory:

`/opt/tu1nz_repos/backups/commercial-s3-1-fix/20260829T13-53-11Z`

It contains the root-private archive, database dump, PostgreSQL globals and
baseline but no completed `SHA256SUMS`; it is not an authorized recovery point
and must remain as aborted diagnostic evidence. At abort, the candidate service
was still inactive/dead with `NRestarts=0` and no process. Application, Control,
unit, S3 state and database remained unchanged.

The correction anchors comparison at `/` with `tar -C / --compare`. A focused
test requires that exact restore-proof boundary. A new recovery directory must
be used after this correction is reviewed, merged and its post-merge CI is
green. The partial directory is never reused.
